# Normalize line endings on the way into the repository.
#
# Everything here is LF in the repository, whatever the machine that commits it
# happens to use. Without this, a Windows checkout stores CRLF and a Linux
# checkout stores LF, so the same commit produces a diff on the other machine —
# and `gradlew` (the shell script, not gradlew.bat) with a CRLF shebang fails to
# run at all on Linux and macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only launcher: CRLF is what cmd.exe and PowerShell expect.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries. `text=auto` would otherwise be allowed to sniff these, and a single
# byte changed in the Gradle wrapper jar stops every clone from building.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary

# GitHub reads these as the repository's language breakdown. Marking the
# vendored jar as binary is not enough — `linguist-vendored` keeps the Gradle
# wrapper out of the "Java 100%" pie chart.
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar linguist-vendored
